/*  EXPECTED: REJECTED at type-check, identically by both backends.
    Region escape via a METHOD called in the POSSESSIVE form — `b's get-items` rather
    than `get-items on (b)`. Same route as escape-method.cufe, a different spelling.

    It was accepted: the possessive form reached the method through a resolved copy of
    its type that had lost the method's return-depth signature, so what it handed back
    was taken to be freshly made. The compiled program then read the series after the
    rabbit's Done. had popped its region, and died with an access violation. */

Define object bag with (the series of number items).

Bind series of number to get-items unto bag:
    return one's items.
Done.

Define outer as a series of number.
Pull a rabbit.
    Define inner as a series of number with (1, 2, 3).
    Define b as a new bag { the items inner }.
    outer becomes Cast b's get-items.
Done.
